
Running the Test Suite:
-----------------------
This project includes test suite covering arbitration logic. 
Tests are located under the Test/ directory and use the Catch2 framework.

Prerequisites
-------------
CMake 3.10 or newer
A C++17‑compatible compiler
Docker (optional, if running tests inside the provided container)
Catch2 is included as a submodule or vendored dependency and is automatically built as part of the test target.

Configuration & Building Tests
---------------------------

run.sh and docker_run.sh will automatically run tests unless --no-test  option is given
But, if we want to run only tests then follow instructions given below:

From the project root:

1. export PCAP_DIR=<Pcap Files Directory> 
   For example:
   > export PCAP_DIR=PcapSamples  
2. Change the desired values in file Test/test_summary.cpp
3. Build 
   >./build.sh

   This  will produce a test executable named:
   run_tests

Running Tests
-------------
From the project directory:
> build/Test/run_tests


Running Tests Inside Docker
---------------------------

From the project directory:
> ./docker_run.sh <Pcap Files Directory> 

It will run test along with main application
 

Adding New Tests
----------------
New test files can be added under:
Test/

They will be automatically included in the build as long as they are listed in Test/CMakeLists.txt.

